 <h2>Read the totals with their assumptions.</h2>
 <p class="guide-body-note">Tax is an illustrative <strong>9.75% reserve</strong> on goods, equipment and fabrication, excluding electricity and shipping. It is not an address-specific tax calculation or a statement about labor taxability. Confirm at checkout with the <a href="https://cdtfa.ca.gov/taxes-and-fees/sales-use-tax-rates.htm">CDTFA lookup</a>. Contingency is 20% of hardware + the spool + shipping. It is not a tested failure rate.</p>
 <p class="guide-body-note">If you already own every suitable equipment/fixture item, the same base model is <strong>{{ money(owned.diyCash) }}</strong>. A printer alone accounts for $549 plus about $53.53 of the illustrative tax reserve. The printer is not a per-chair recurring charge.</p>

 <p class="guide-body-note">The shop quote must include metric tube supply, plate material, hole finishes, spacers, retention and any assembly fixtures. Ask shock and wheel suppliers to approve the actual interface drawing and intended use. No shock spring rate, compatible SKU or harness-anchor design is released by this budget.</p>
