 <h2>Time and review are real costs.</h2><div class="guide-table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Cost comparison, scroll horizontally on small screens" tabindex="0"><table class="guide-table"><thead><tr><th>Additional allowance</th><th>Basis</th><th class="money">Low</th><th class="money">Base</th><th class="money">High</th></tr></thead><tbody>@foreach (developmentAllowances as line)<tr><td><strong>{{ line.name }}</strong></td><td>{{ line.basis }}</td><td class="money">{{ money(line.low) }}</td><td class="money">{{ money(line.base) }}</td><td class="money">{{ money(line.high) }}</td></tr>@endforeach<tr class="total-row"><td colspan="2">DIY cash + paid assembly + development</td><td class="money">{{ money(cases[0].developmentBudget) }}</td><td class="money">{{ money(base.developmentBudget) }}</td><td class="money">{{ money(cases[2].developmentBudget) }}</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
 <div class="guide-callout"><strong>This does not buy a safety approval.</strong> Review scope and test results are unresolved. More iterations, custom shocks, guarding, harness-anchor redesign, durability studies or failed specimens can exceed every allowance. Veterinary treatment and ongoing care, product liability/insurance, business overhead and production certification are not included.</div>
 <h2>What is verified, and what still needs a quote.</h2><ol class="guide-source-list"><li><a href="https://additiveplus.com/product/bambu-lab-p2s/">Additive Plus P2S listing</a>: $549 printer-only configuration, listed November 8, 2026. Confirm the exact configuration, stock, freight and checkout price. No AMS assumed.</li><li><a href="https://www.harborfreight.com/6-in-digital-caliper-63711.html">Harbor Freight 63711</a>: $24.99 regular price. No membership or coupon assumed. These calipers are for parts, not Buddy’s body.</li><li><a href="https://www.sunlu.com/products/filadryer-s2-filament-dryer">SUNLU S2 manufacturer specification</a> and <a href="https://shop.polymaker.com/products/petg">Polymaker PETG product information</a> are capability references. Their current prices/configurations were not verified for this model. Dryer and filament are allowances.</li><li>All metalwork, pins, wheels, shocks, softgoods, labor and professional services require quotes. The shock and harness-anchor interfaces do not yet have approved purchasable parts.</li></ol>
 <h2>Before committing money.</h2><ol class="guide-method-list"><li>Finish Buddy’s measurement worksheet and clinical suitability review. Do not map groin height directly to CAD rail height.</li><li>Have the structural drawings, shock/wheel interfaces and harness anchors reviewed. Obtain itemized quotes against the exact configured revision, including material, finish fits, shipping and tax.</li><li>Slice the actual nonstructural meshes on the selected printer. Confirm orientation, build envelope, grams, supports and failed-print allowance. Do not shrink parts to fit a smaller bed.</li><li>Approve an empty-rig test protocol before adding ballast or an animal. Price the resulting revisions; a printed part or a costly printer does not establish capacity.</li></ol>
 <p class="guide-body-note">The storefront’s $264.50 XL price is a future retail planning target. Its $155 production COGS envelope is unquoted and excludes this one-off custom suspension development. Neither figure is the build cost above, and this r0 package has not demonstrated that retail target.</p>
 <footer class="guide-footer"><span>Model source: app/Designs/PrototypeBudget.ts · cents rounded once per reserve.</span><span>buddywheels.org/prototype-budget · 4 / 4</span></footer>
